A task with `status: blocked` is explicitly parked. It has no unmet *graph*
blockers, so it used to be announced as ready, the tool contradicting its own
plan. Only the genuinely workable task is listed.

```
$ aplan ready
D-002  Actually workable (2d)

```

```
$ aplan why D-001
D-001 is `blocked`: explicitly parked, not waiting on the graph. What it waits on is in the task body; no field carries it

```

```
$ aplan check
ok: 2 tasks, 0 warning(s), DAG acyclic

```
